RgMqtt - an MQTT 3.1.1 client package for Regina Rexx
=====================================================

RgMqtt lets Rexx programs talk to an MQTT broker (Mosquitto, HiveMQ, EMQX,
the brokers of IoT platforms, ...). It is an external function package
like RegUtil: the shared library librgmqtt.so (rgmqtt.dll in the Windows zip),
built and installed together with Regina. It needs nothing but the system's
sockets. TLS is not supported; use a local TLS tunnel (stunnel) or a broker
listener without TLS.

External function packages are loaded by the dynamic interpreter `regina`
(which uses libregina; in the Windows zip regina.exe with regina.dll and
rgmqtt.dll). The standalone `rexx` executables (the static Linux build, the
Windows rexx.exe and the macOS build) can't load packages.

To try it without a broker of your own, use the public test server
test.mosquitto.org of the Eclipse Mosquitto project: port 1883 without a
password, or 1884 with user "rw" and password "readwrite" (the TLS ports
can't be used). Everybody can read what is published there.
demo/mqtt/15_public_broker.rexx does this; 13_mqtt.rexx and
14_mqtt_oo.rexx take a host and port.

Loading
-------

    call RxFuncAdd 'MqttLoadFuncs', 'rgmqtt', 'MqttLoadFuncs'
    call MqttLoadFuncs

In OO programs `::requires 'mqtt'` gives the classes Mqtt and MqttMessage,
which load the functions themselves (see below).

Functions
---------

MqttConnect(host [,port] [,clientid] [,options.])
    Connects and returns a handle (a whole number), or 0 if the connection
    failed (MqttError() says why). port defaults to 1883. Without a client
    id one is generated. options. is the name of a stem whose tails set:
      KEEPALIVE    seconds between pings (default 60, 0 = none)
      CLEAN        1 (default) a clean session, 0 keep the session
      USER, PASSWORD
      WILLTOPIC, WILLMESSAGE, WILLQOS, WILLRETAIN
                   the message the broker publishes when the connection
                   breaks without MqttDisconnect
      TIMEOUT      seconds to wait for an acknowledgement (default 10)

MqttPublish(h, topic, message [,qos] [,retain])
    Publishes message (any bytes) with QoS 0 (default), 1 or 2. retain 1
    keeps it on the broker for later subscribers (an empty retained
    message removes it). Returns 0, or -1 on error. QoS 1 and 2 wait for
    the broker's acknowledgement.

MqttSubscribe(h, filter [,qos])
    Subscribes to a topic filter (+ and # are wildcards). Returns the QoS
    the broker granted, 128 if it refused, -1 on error.

MqttUnsubscribe(h, filter)
    Returns 0, or -1 on error.

MqttReceive(h, stem. [,seconds])
    Returns 1 and sets stem.TOPIC, stem.MESSAGE, stem.QOS, stem.RETAIN and
    stem.DUP when a message arrived within seconds (default 0: only those
    already received; decimals allowed), 0 if none came, -1 if the
    connection was lost. Messages that arrive while another call waits for
    an acknowledgement are queued; MqttReceive returns them in order.

MqttPending(h)
    The number of received messages MqttReceive has not returned yet.

MqttPing(h)
    A round trip to the broker: 0, or -1 if the connection is lost.
    Keep-alive pings are sent automatically while RgMqtt waits.

MqttDisconnect(h)
    Disconnects (the will is not published). Returns 0.

MqttError()
    The text of the last error, empty after a successful MqttConnect.

MqttVersion(), MqttDropFuncs()

A lost connection is closed; later calls with its handle return -1 with
"not a connection handle". Wrong arguments (a QoS of 3, say) raise error
40, "Incorrect call to routine".

Example
-------

    call RxFuncAdd 'MqttLoadFuncs', 'rgmqtt', 'MqttLoadFuncs'
    call MqttLoadFuncs
    opt.user = 'rexx'; opt.password = 'secret'
    opt.willtopic = 'status/rexx'; opt.willmessage = 'offline'
    h = MqttConnect('broker.example.com', 1883, 'rexx-1', 'opt.')
    if h = 0 then do; say 'no connection:' MqttError(); exit 1; end
    call MqttSubscribe h, 'sensors/#', 1
    call MqttPublish h, 'status/rexx', 'online', 1, 1
    do while MqttReceive(h, 'msg.', 30)
      say msg.topic '=' msg.message
    end
    call MqttDisconnect h

The Mqtt class (OO programs)
----------------------------

    c = .mqtt~connect('localhost')                 -- .nil if it failed
    if c == .nil then do; say .mqtt~error; exit 1; end
    c~subscribe('sensors/#', 1)
    c~publish('sensors/kitchen', 21.5, 1)
    n = c~listen({ use arg m; say m~topic '=' m~message }, 5)
    c~disconnect
    ::requires 'mqtt'

.mqtt~connect(host [,port] [,clientid] [,options]) takes the options as a
Directory (keepAlive, user, password, willTopic, ...). An Mqtt object has
publish (1 or 0), subscribe (granted QoS, -1 if refused), unsubscribe,
receive([seconds]) (an MqttMessage with topic, message, qos, retain, dup,
or .nil), listen(block [,seconds]) (calls the block for every message
until none comes for seconds, forever if omitted, or the block returns
0; returns the number of messages), pending, ping, isConnected, error
and disconnect.

Tests
-----

tests/packages/mqtt_functions.rexx and mqtt_class.rexx run against
tests/packages/minibroker.py (a small broker written for the tests) in the
"packages" suite of tests/run-regression.sh. RgMqtt was also checked
against Mosquitto 2.0 and its mosquitto_pub/mosquitto_sub clients.
